Preview this file to check the Rouge code paths. Every block below must render
as `<pre class="highlight">`; none may raise.

The first three reach `Rouge::Lexer.lookup_fancy`, which called `CGI.parse`
until rouge 4.6.1 — the path that broke under Ruby 4.0.


# No language tag

```
puts "hello"
```


# Indented (redcarpet always passes nil here)

    puts "hello"


# Lexer options

```erb?parent=html
<%= 1 + 1 %>
```


# Tagged — highlighted, and never touched CGI

```ruby
puts "hello"
```


# Unknown tag — falls back to plain text

```nosuchlexer
puts "hello"
```
